  "reviewPerformed": [
    "Read the full new runtime matcher and all four new test modules as source text.",
    "Independently inspected actual three-file before/candidate diffs for server, client and README. Changes outside those scoped diffs were not inferred from the authoring script.",
    "Read the pinned original standalone parser, relevant full query-builder functions and SearchEngine normalization/search call paths; preserved corrected exact upstream SHA-256 values.",
    "Read the synthetic DOM fixture to verify its hook runs after the genuine server handler result and its held-response control discriminates earlier matching versus newer empty results.",
    "Read the complete study plan and notice, inspect source provenance, and independently check all 18 final file byte/SHA identities.",
    "Independently compare all 41 baseline Notes source byte counts and SHA-256 values against the provenance roster: zero mismatches."
  ],
  "integrationFindings": [
    "Omitted mode still selects simple. Its lowercasing, whitespace tokens, AND substring haystack over title/body/tag/notebook, selectors, updated-time ordering and preview token remain equivalent in the inspected diff.",
    "Filters requires explicit mode selection, validates mode and query, uses a separate predicate, and leaves persistence/edit/export code untouched. Existing selectors remain AND restrictions.",
    "Client adds one labeled select, passes its value to list, invokes the existing read-only refresh path, and includes the new select in notebook-operation disabling/restoration.",
    "The existing two refresh-generation guards remain in place. The held-positive-response DOM case tests earlier A-note results against a newer zero-note type filter, so stale result publication would fail its assertions.",
    "Integration cases inspect exact persisted snapshots and write counts for successful and rejected searches, simple-mode equality, independent selectors and trash boundaries.",
    "Previously raised empty-field and empty-substring policies are now explicitly described in README and plan and covered by candidate test source. They are disclosed local behavior, not FTS parity."
  ],
  "originalComparisonFindings": [
    "Original parser and builder bytes are checked against exact byte counts, SHA-256 and Git blob identities before TypeScript-only transformation and module import in the future hosted test.",
    "All original builder function bodies are retained. Exactly one known date-service import is replaced with a deny-on-access Proxy; metadata-only cases must not use this adapter. There is no fallback oracle.",
    "The metadata comparison creates a separate in-memory SQLite database and executes original generated SQL with useFts=false. Candidate note-ID sets are independently computed on the corresponding records.",
    "The 32-case metadata corpus discriminates duplicate notebook titles, recursive descendants, exclusions, absent scopes, independent type/completion, tag presence/absence, percent/underscore/star wildcards and distinct non-ASCII case.",
    "The 48-case parser corpus includes successful syntax and thrown errors, partial quotes, unsupported parsed filters, unknown filter fallback, negation, empty fields, tabs, colon retention and wildcard representation.",
    "These are authored comparisons, not observed passing results. Their adapters do not execute the complete original database lifecycle, FTS, application or GUI."
  ],
